<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William Sayle</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1590–<a href="/years/1671">1671</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William Sayle was an English Puritan colonist and governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bermuda">Bermuda</a> who in 1648 led the Eleutheran Adventurers, settlers from Bermuda seeking religious freedom, to found a colony on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eleuthera">Eleuthera</a> in the Bahamas. In old age he was appointed the first governor of the Province of Carolina, sailing with the settlers who founded Charles Town in 1670, and died in office in 1671.</p></div>
